 "review": "Independent review: OK (writes copy-on-write safe within a record; equality unaffected; split cost once per match start); follow-ups (an in-record write test, two comments) prepared, not gated.",
 "notes": "Behaviour equal (all 10 scenarios, AppKit, unchecked, emulator, frames identical; 10 suites). A12 with music and sounds: end PSS 504-510 against 545-592 MiB, native heap dirty 453 against 489-532, peak 588-593 against 596-626 (overlapping), load, launch to loaded and frame time overlapping. Mac: live heap 15 MB lower (the replay pages), but phys_footprint higher: at the loaded event 670-682 against 556-598 MiB and at body 600 698-711 against 605-644 in the gate and in a repeat A/B; vmmap without stack logging shows L20's Malloc Small has ~48 MB resident but clean (freed memory macOS malloc marked reusable) where M9's is all dirty, plus 28 MB of dirty empty Malloc Large regions: the pages M9 copies on first write, scattered in time, keep macOS malloc from returning memory freed after the load. With the user's decision to stop the loop (2026-10-11), M9 is not merged: a memory change that measurably raises one host's footprint needs that explained or avoided first.",
